Licensed under Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE).

Source: https://github.com/HybridRobotics/supermimic
Reference commit: abc124c1bd5976341034668af3d12c087f2f1f55
Paper: Qiayuan Liao et al. (2026), SuperMimic: Scaling Humanoid Whole-Body
Control with One Differentiable World Model. https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.28480

The optional velocity-only dynamics, fixed physical loss tolerances, structured
critic, visited-bin return curriculum and graph-storage validation adapt designs
or algorithms from representations.py, learners/wm_learner.py,
learners/learner_utils.py, models.py,
envs/world_model_env.py and runners/reset_sampling.py.

Modified for this repository: retained robot state/action conventions, explicit
root velocity loss, full policy-history encoding, segment-local sampling and
checkpoint persistence, finite-update guards and flat observations.
No separate upstream runner or mjlab fork is bundled.


SuperMimic-Reproduced
====================

The optional world-model integration prior, motion encoder design, terminal-state
recording, execution-only noise, distributed gradient averaging, evaluation/drift
protocol and numerical validation ideas were adapted from or informed by:

  CuboiLeo/SuperMimic-Reproduced
  https://github.com/CuboiLeo/SuperMimic-Reproduced
  Reference commit: ba6105349069bf040f1fdad60873d13138d505a2

These features implement or extend the method described in:

  Qiayuan Liao et al. (2026), SuperMimic: Scaling Humanoid Whole-Body Control
  with One Differentiable World Model. https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.28480

The reproduced code is an independent implementation, not the paper authors'
official code. File-level comments identify the relevant upstream source paths.
The upstream license notice is preserved below. The rest of wbc-mjlab remains
under its existing Apache-2.0 license.

