xMimic and draft disturbance adaptation
======================================

The optional tracking-based imagined termination in rl/wm/termination.py is
adapted from BlinkMimic's sigmoid termination relaxation and its xMimic port:
  https://github.com/nico-bohlinger/xmimic
  Reference commit: 54860e100251fa80143627565568d5e6b0ff2c2b
  Source: xmimic/mdp.py, soft_termination
It uses this repository's task thresholds and the existing SuperMimic trainer;
xMimic's JAX execution pipeline is not incorporated.

rl/wm/perturbations.py reuses the user's draft_wbc velocity-kick controller,
adapted to the shared environment, replay and checkpoint contracts. Its original
precedent is BlinkMimic env.py / buffer.py at
d264658d6c9ce61fb52f9f0f8985a369f3ccc409.

